INT. PARKING STRUCTURE ROOFTOP - DAWN

A rental van. Two women lean on its bumper. Between them, a gym bag.

LEONIE ASANTEWAA-VOGEL (40s, bomber jacket) lights a cigarette. Her hands are steady.

MARGUERETTA "RETTA" OKOYE-BLOOM (30s, hoodie) watches the sun come up over a gray city.

Leonie offers the pack. Retta shakes her head.

LEONIE
You hungry?

RETTA
No.

LEONIE
You should eat.

RETTA
Later.

Leonie drags on the cigarette. Looks at the bag.

LEONIE
She wanted it split three ways.

RETTA
She wanted a lot of things.

LEONIE
She called me last night.

RETTA
She called me, too.

Silence. A pigeon lands on the van roof. Walks the length of it.

LEONIE
She said she was sorry.

RETTA
She said that to me, too.

Leonie flicks the ash. Retta stares at her shoes.

LEONIE
Nobody's coming.

RETTA
I know.

LEONIE
So we could just go.

RETTA
We could.

Neither moves. The pigeon takes off.

Retta bends. Unzips the bag a few inches. Looks. Zips it shut. She hands the strap to Leonie, and Leonie takes it, and for a moment neither lets go.

LEONIE
Which way?

RETTA
You pick.

Leonie opens the van door. Retta gets in. Leonie follows. They sit with the engine off and the sun on the windshield.
